# 4. AUTHENTICATION

Implement Firebase Authentication.

Support:

- Mobile number authentication
- Email/password authentication where appropriate
- Password reset
- Account verification
- Session management
- Account status

During development, allow mobile registration without requiring OTP.

However, the architecture must already support:

```text
mobileNumber
phoneVerified
email
emailVerified
verificationStatus
```

so real OTP verification can be enabled later.

Never store passwords directly in Firestore.

---

# 5. USER ROLES

HEMORA has four roles:

```text
DONOR
HOSPITAL
STAFF
ADMIN
```

Role information must be securely associated with the authenticated Firebase user.

Use Firebase Custom Claims for authorization-sensitive role checks where appropriate.

Firestore data must never rely solely on frontend role selection.

The backend must independently verify:

```text
Firebase UID
Authentication status
Role
Account status
Resource ownership
Permissions
```

A user must never gain permissions simply by modifying frontend code or API requests.

---

# 6. ROLE-BASED ACCESS CONTROL

Implement strict RBAC.

## DONOR

Can:

- View own profile
- Update allowed profile information
- View own appointments
- Book appointment
- Reschedule appointment
- Cancel appointment
- View own donation history
- View own notifications
- View donation-related information
- Manage own voluntary donation appointments

Cannot:

- Create blood requests
- Modify inventory
- Approve requests
- Access hospital data
- Access other donor records
- Record donations
- Perform medical screening
- Issue blood
- Modify blood units

---

## HOSPITAL

Can:

- Manage own hospital profile
- Manage own doctors
- Create blood requests
- View own requests
- Track request status
- Create emergency requests
- Receive notifications
- Confirm receipt
- Record discrepancies
- View own reports

Cannot:

- Modify inventory
- Approve its own requests
- Add blood units
- Modify donor records
- Approve hospitals
- Access other hospitals' private data

---

## STAFF

Can:

- Manage donors
- Manage donor appointments
- Perform screening
- Record donations
- Record testing results
- Manage blood units
- Manage inventory
- Process requests
- Handle emergency requests
- Reserve blood
- Dispatch blood
- Record issue/dispatched details
- Manage appointment capacity
- View operational reports

Cannot:

- Change global administrator settings unless explicitly permitted
- Create administrator accounts
- Modify audit history
- Bypass critical authorization controls

---

## ADMIN

Full supervision privileges.

Can:

- Manage users
- Manage hospitals
- Manage staff
- Approve/reject hospitals
- Supervise inventory
- Supervise emergency requests
- Review audit logs
- Configure thresholds
- Configure escalation timers
- View reports
- Manage system settings
- Intervene in workflows
- Manage role permissions where appropriate

Audit logs must remain protected from modification/deletion.

